{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_155947_1d6de5", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Subject: Cloud-first IT: managing a hybrid fleet across three offices\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nI know your team already runs cloud-hosted workstations for CAD and simulation. But what about the time engineers spend on site where connectivity is unreliable?\n\nWhen field staff can't reach the cloud, productivity stalls. A local machine that handles the same workloads ensures continuity.\n\nI'm not suggesting replacing your cloud setup. I'm proposing a hybrid fleet that covers the gaps.\n\nWould you be open to a 15-minute conversation next week? I can show you how a few well-chosen devices can keep your team productive offline.\n\nBest,\n\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\nSubject: Keeping client data under your control\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nSecurity is a priority. You want client project data under your firm's control, not dependent on a vendor's network.\n\nThe Aurora 14 AI Workstation ships with TPM 2.0 and a self-healing BIOS. These features keep local data encrypted and protect against firmware-level threats.\n\nIt also includes a fingerprint reader and IR camera for biometric authentication. This adds a layer of security beyond your cloud credentials.\n\nWould you be willing to see the full security specifications in a brief document?\n\nBest,\n\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\nSubject: Q1 budget: a hybrid fleet that fits your cycle\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nYour budget closes at the end of Q1. Anything not approved waits a year.\n\nThe Aurora 14 AI Workstation starts at $2,899. It includes an 86 Wh battery with up to 11 hours of local video playback. This means engineers can work all day on a single charge, even in remote sites.\n\nIt also has 32 GB of standard memory, configurable up to 128 GB, and two M.2 storage slots. You can upgrade it as your AI needs grow.\n\nShall we schedule a meeting next week to discuss how this fits your Q1 budget?\n\nBest,\n\n[Your Name]", "tokens": {"input": 847, "output": 421, "total": 5087, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 52342, "timestamp": 1790809239930}